"""A spelling-continuation feature after d (Latin, Cyrillic, Arabic, or Thai).

Single vowels, apostrophes, and grammatical endings usually give a positive
response. Other word fragments, especially those starting i/u, give a weak
negative response. Short preceding pieces ending in d strengthen the effect.
This approximates the sparse spelling pattern, not small background activity.
