"""A local grammatical-role cue, strongest on personal pronouns.

Clause openers and sentence punctuation give a negative signal; prepositions,
object-taking verbs and inverted auxiliaries give a positive one. Demonstratives
and indefinite pronouns have a weaker, mostly negative response. Token case and
leading space distinguish sentence pronouns from fragments of larger words.
Small multilingual pronoun sets use the same rough role cue. Unlisted tokens
return zero. Only the preceding token is remembered, with a document reset.
The word-class scores approximate the measurements, not a full syntactic parse.
"""
READS = ()

# Each group describes how the previous word frames the following pronoun.
